!!id:"https://tson.io/test-suite/schemas/fixtures/validate-positional-name.tn"
!!meta:"https://tson.io/2026/39/m/meta.tn"
!!import:"https://tson.io/2026/39/m/core.tn"
@doc:"""
  A fixture schema for the class2/validate layer: records with one field each, so a data document fills that field
  positionally. `cell`'s one field is an atom; `slot`'s is `type`, a `kind<record>` through core.tn's own `kind`,
  whose values are the names of the record types in this schema's closure. A data document has no namespace of its
  own, so a bare token fills each of them positionally; the kind-typed one is then judged a member in the governing
  schema's namespace, where a data document's kind values resolve. A field typed by one of the kernel's own records
  (`type_ref`, `record_field`) has no place here: an ordinary schema imports only ordinary ones, so such a field
  exists only in a document the meta-kernel governs.
  """
{
  cell   => { value: integer }
  slot   => { type: kind<record> }
  holder => { c?: cell  s?: slot }
}
